# SABOTAGE: O4 (ADR-045 §4.2) — the generated aud_event REVOKE role RE-HARDCODED to "clank". The
# fix made `m_aud_event.eex` derive the app role at migration time (the :aud_event_app_role knob,
# else the repo's configured :username, else RAISE) instead of defaulting to the literal "clank"
# — a developer's local Postgres role that would ship `REVOKE UPDATE, DELETE ON aud_event FROM
# clank` into every adopter's prod migration (whose first release_command then aborts). This
# sabotage restores the "clank" default, so the rendered migration once again contains the laptop
# role. The named O4 red path (the generated migration must NOT contain "clank") MUST flip.
# APP: samen_core
# TEST_FILES: test/gen_deploy_bootability_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: the generated aud_event migration derives the DB app role, never a hardcoded 'clank' (O4)
diff --git a/samen_core/priv/templates/m_aud_event.eex b/samen_core/priv/templates/m_aud_event.eex
index 9df5a91..a8685e3 100644
--- a/samen_core/priv/templates/m_aud_event.eex
+++ b/samen_core/priv/templates/m_aud_event.eex
@@ -13,7 +13,7 @@ defmodule <%= module %>.Repo.Migrations.AudEvent do
   #   3. RAISE a named error — refusing to guess a role, since a REVOKE against the WRONG role
